From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 21:18:28 +0200
Subject: media: ov5640: Put unity in the middle of the image control sliders

The saturation and the contrast are gains whose unity sits well below
the register maximum - 0x40 and 0x20 - so a range running to 255 put
unity a quarter and an eighth of the way along and squeezed everything
usable into the bottom of the slider. The same thing was reported on the
gc2145 as the controls being exponential.

Chroma and luma clip long before the top of that range, so nothing is
lost by stopping at twice unity, which is also more than the vendor
settings ever ask for: they reach 0x60 of saturation and 0x2c of
contrast.

The brightness is a signed luma offset and already centred, so it keeps
the whole range its register can express.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c | 19 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5640.c
@@ -3981,15 +3981,30 @@ static int ov5640_init_controls(struct ov5640_dev *sensor)
 					      V4L2_AUTO_FOCUS_STATUS_FAILED),
 					     0, V4L2_AUTO_FOCUS_STATUS_IDLE);
 
+	/*
+	 * Both of these are gains with a unity well below the register
+	 * maximum, so a range that runs to 255 puts unity at a quarter and
+	 * an eighth of the way along and squeezes everything usable into
+	 * the bottom of the slider. Chroma and luma clip long before the
+	 * top of that range is reached anyway. Stop at twice unity, which
+	 * puts it in the middle and still covers more than the vendor
+	 * settings ever ask for - they reach 0x60 of saturation and 0x2c
+	 * of contrast.
+	 */
 	ctrls->saturation = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_SATURATION,
-					      0, 255, 1,
+					      0, OV5640_SATURATION_UNITY * 2, 1,
 					      OV5640_SATURATION_UNITY);
 	ctrls->hue = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_HUE,
 				       0, 359, 1, 0);
+	/*
+	 * The brightness is a signed luma offset and is already centred, so
+	 * it keeps the whole range the register can express.
+	 */
 	ctrls->brightness = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_BRIGHTNESS,
 					      -255, 255, 1, 0);
 	ctrls->contrast = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_CONTRAST,
-					    0, 255, 1, OV5640_CONTRAST_UNITY);
+					    0, OV5640_CONTRAST_UNITY * 2, 1,
+					    OV5640_CONTRAST_UNITY);
 	ctrls->test_pattern =
 		v4l2_ctrl_new_std_menu_items(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_TEST_PATTERN,
 					     ARRAY_SIZE(test_pattern_menu) - 1,
